== (3) the never-descending set K and the integers ==
 negative odd integers n >= -10^5 in K (word never descends): [-1, -5, -17]
 positive odd n <= 10^5 in K: [] (1 is not in K: its word (2)^inf descends at once); record first word-descent: n = 35655 at odd step 85
 reading: Collatz over Z is the statement K cap Z = {-1, -5, -17}; K is a closed 2-adic set of Hausdorff dimension h(log_3 2) = 0.95 (sibling ladder Thm 1a) that contains three negative integers and, conjecturally, no positive one: the distinction is the sign, invisible 2-adically
